          <caption>
            <p>Occult Metastasis on Advanced Nuclear Imaging. This sagittal fused fluorodeoxyglucose positron emission tomography/computed tomography (FDG PET/CT) image of a 56-year-old patient shows a highly FDG-avid (SUV max 18) mass of the midthoracic esophagus (green arrow) with solitary metastasis in the L2 vertebral body (yellow arrow).&#x000a0;FDG PET/CT identified a metastatic lesion that was not detected on the staging CT scan, resulting in an upstaging of the disease. Contributed by Dr Amaila Ramzan, FRCR</p>
